{
  "name": "Roland DJ-202",
  "author": "The OpenDJ contributors",
  "description": "Two-deck mapping for the Roland DJ-202. Control assignments were taken from Roland's MIDI implementation chart and cross checked against the Mixxx community mapping by Silvio Ankermann, Sebastian Reusse and Rene Kraus (https://github.com/mixxxdj/mixxx/wiki/Roland-Dj-202), which is GPLv2 or later and so compatible with this project. The DJ-202 powers up in a standalone mode in which it sends nothing at all; initMessages asks it to talk to a computer, and keepAlive holds it there, since it falls back after about a second and a half without one. The platters report relative ticks on CC 0x06, centred on 64. They also stream 14-bit absolute position as pitch bend on 0xE0/0xE1, but that flows whenever a hand merely rests on the wheel, so it is deliberately left unmapped. Pressing DECK moves a side onto MIDI channels 3 and 4; those are routed back to the same decks, so a stray press cannot leave one dead. LOOP IN and LOOP OUT set a loop by hand, and the parameter buttons beside them halve and double it. The browse encoder scrolls the library and the load buttons put the selected track on a deck. Deck-toggle, effects, the TR-S sequencer and the pad modes beyond hot cue are recognised by the hardware but not yet mapped here.",
  "deviceNameHints": [
    "DJ-202",
    "DJ202"
  ],
  "jogTicksPerRevolution": 800,
  "initMessages": [
    "F0 00 20 7F 00 F7",
    "F0 00 20 7F 01 F7"
  ],
  "keepAlive": {
    "message": "BF 64 00",
    "intervalMs": 500
  },
